{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.delta_max_numerical_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.delta_max_numerical_scale","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L28-L40","doc":"**Numerical scale of the uniform bound.**  From the uniform bound on\n`|Δ_max|`, the two-sided enclosure `-bound ≤ Δ_max ≤ bound` follows,\nand the bound is strictly positive so the enclosing interval is\nnon-degenerate.\n\n§3b-conditional on `DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext`: the bound itself is\nassumed, not established.  The conclusion is *derived* from the\nhypothesis fields rather than projected from a conclusion field, so\nthis is not a self-assuming projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:delta-max-numerical-scale","label":"prop:delta-max-numerical-scale","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/delta-max-numerical-scale.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.deltaMax_abs_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.deltaMax_abs_le","kind":"theorem","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L26-L26","doc":"The uniform bound holds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.deltaMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.deltaMax","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L24-L24","doc":"The quantity being bounded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.bound_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.bound_pos","kind":"theorem","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L22-L22","doc":"The bound is a genuine (positive) scale. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.bound","kind":"def","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L20-L20","doc":"The uniform bound on the jet-filtration defect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":18,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L18-L18","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Appendix.DeltaMaxNumericalScale.DeltaMaxNumericalScaleContext","kind":"class","line":5,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Appendix/DeltaMaxNumericalScale.lean#L5-L26","doc":"Context for the uniform `Δ_max` scale bound.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-21** (vacuity ledger, `proof-no-trivial-true` /\n`reflexive-tautology-ascribed-literal`).  The class previously carried\nthe single field `holds : (1 : ℝ) = 1` — provable by `rfl`, so it\nconstrained no instance at all, and the theorem below projected it to\nconclude `(1 : ℝ) = 1`: vacuous with *or* without an instance.\n\nThe fields now state the actual hypothesis the appendix block names —\nthat `Δ_max` is uniformly bounded by a positive scale.  The bound is\ncarried as a **parameter**, not a numeral: the block's numerical value\nis not derived anywhere in the corpus, and inventing one here would be\na fit.  Supplying it is the open work (bean `qou-7fyw`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}